    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1983-p21.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(100\\gt99,\\) choice A is positive; since \\(324\\lt325,\\) choice C is negative; and since \\(2601\\gt2600,\\) choice D is positive while E is negative. The two positive values satisfy \\[ \\begin{aligned} 10-3\\sqrt{11} &=\\frac1{10+3\\sqrt{11}},\\\\ 51-10\\sqrt{26} &=\\frac1{51+10\\sqrt{26}}. \\end{aligned} \\] The second denominator is larger, so choice D is the smaller positive number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Compare the squares to determine which listed differences are positive",
        "Rationalize each positive difference using \\(a-b=\\frac{a^2-b^2}{a+b}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
